7.20.3 Any absence from campus affecti","According to Article 7.20 – ABSENCE - GENERAL, the rules concerning absence are as follows:

* The University requires its members to be available on a regular and ongoing basis to ensure that activities can be carried out in an orderly manner (Article 7.20.1).
* Any absence shall not normally interfere with assigned and/or scheduled activities and the harmonious functioning of the Department/School (Article 7.20.2).
* Absences from campus affecting teaching/professional librarian duties should not occur, as they can disrupt the University's operations ( Article 7.20.3).

It is also noted that general grievances related to absence must be brought to the attention of the President and the Thorneloe Steward before a formal grievance can be submitted (Article 7.20.7).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.7443,17.8557,50.2406,4374.0,292.7,1.0,,,bridge
