(16) additional weeks",91be281d-0a04-4e95-bef5-23aaa3df2717,0.353,0.2824,0.0159,"14.06 Congé d’adoption
À l’occasion de l’adoption d’un enfant, tout membre qui est le parent et qui a choisi de prendre un congé parental en vertu
de la Loi sur l’assurance-emploi et de toute autre loi applicable aura droit à un congé parental d’une durée maximale de
trente-cinq (35) semaines.
Pendant la durée du congé d’adoption, le membre recevra de l’Employeur 100 % de son salaire nominal pendant cinq
jours après que le membre a travaillé pendant un minimum de 12 mois consécutifs.","The Collective Agreement 2017-2020 provides the following regarding pregnancy, parental, and adoption leaves:

* A pregnant full-time Member or pregnant Master Lecturer Member is entitled to 17 weeks of pregnancy leave (Article 7.60.1).
* During the period of pregnancy leave, the Member shall receive:
 + 100% of her nominal salary for the first week.
 + Up to a maximum of 16 additional weeks (Article 7.60.1.b).
* A Member who is not entitled to take parental leave and has a newborn child in the hospital may postpone or interrupt her pregnancy leave by the number of weeks the newborn child is hospitalized, but must take it within 52 weeks from the date of birth.
* The pregnancy leave ends on the later of:
 + 17 weeks after the pregnancy leave began (Article 7.60.1.b).
 + 6 weeks after the birth of the child.

Regarding adoption leaves, the Collective Agreement provides:

* A Member who is a parent and chooses to take parental leave in accordance with the Employment Insurance Act and other applicable laws has the right to an adoption leave of up to 35 weeks.
* During the period of adoption leave, the Member receives 100% of her nominal salary for five days after working a minimum of 12 consecutive months. (Article 14.06)",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.3049,3.5508,55.9676,4376.0,299.0,,,,bridge
