President, Academic and Provost and the
Dean/University Librarian, after consultation with a Departme",f4bd4186-9137-49f2-bb99-66d3ad7527c9,0.0164,0.0115,0.0164,"Following an adequate investigation, the Vice-President, Academic and
Provost may request the Chair/Director to relinquish their office. If the Chair/Director are not requested to relinquish their
office the Department/School or the
Dean/University Librarian may request initiation of procedures under paragraph 9.30.3 (c) below.
9.30.3 If the Chair/Director does not voluntarily resign as
Chair/Director:
(a) The Vice-President, Academic and Provost is empowered to suspend that individual as
Chair/","According to Article 9.15 – Selection of Chairs/Directors, the definition and description of the selection process for Chair/Directors are as follows:

* The Chair/Director shall be a tenured or probationary Member of faculty (Article 9.15.12).
* The appointment and renewal of Chair/Directors is made in accordance with Article 5.20 – Appointment and Renewal (Article 9.15.12).
* In exceptional circumstances, the Vice-President, Academic and Provost and the Dean/University Librarian may appoint an acting Chair/Director for a period of up to four months, consistent with Article 9.20 – Term of Office of Chairs/Directors and Article 9.30 – Removal from Office (Article 9.15.13).
* The abbreviated selection process allows for direct appointment if a strong consensus emerges in step 4 (Article 9.15.14). If at least two Members object to the abbreviated process, the full procedure shall be followed.
* The term of office for Chairs/Directors is normally three years, renewable by Department/School selection per Article 9.15 – Selection of Chairs/Directors (Article 9.20.1).
* Should Chair/Directors not be able to carry out their duties for four months or less, they shall make provision for the take-over of their duties in consultation with the Department/School and Dean/University Librarian (Article 9.20.2).

Additionally, Article 9.15 – Selection of Chairs/Directors outlines the procedures for selecting Chair/Directors, including:

* The selection committee shall follow the full procedure if at least two Members object to the abbreviated selection process.
* The Vice-President, Academic and Provost may request the Chair/Director to relinquish their office in exceptional circumstances.
* If the Chair/Director does not voluntarily resign, the Dean/University Librarian may initiate procedures under paragraph 9.30.3 (c) below.

The agreement also defines the role of an Acting-Chair/Director, who shall receive a pro-rated stipend in lieu of the Chair/Director for each full month served in excess of the first month (Article 9.25.2).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.9378,3.0055,235.7587,4616.0,318.9,,,,bridge
