5.75.6 When the Vice-President, Academic and Provost is sat",703c73c4-ec2f-4e1a-84b2-6f3528e53bbd,0.3795,0.37,0.0159,"B) Scholarly Activity
5.15.20 Members shall have the right and responsibility to devote a reasonable proportion of their time to scholarly
activity.
5.15.21 It is understood that for the purposes of this Forced Contract the term ""scholarly activity"" means:
(a) Research directed towards a contribution to knowledge, and the dissemination of its results; and/or
(b) Participation in those academic activities that contribute to the enhancement, creation and
dissemination of knowledge; and/or
(c) Crea","According to Article 5.60 - DISCIPLINARY MEASURES, discipline is defined as ""Disciplinary action shall be only for cause. The disciplinary action shall be just and reasonable and be commensurate with the offense."" (Article 4.60)

Additionally, the agreement outlines specific forms of discipline that can be taken against Members, including:

* A formal reprimand in writing
* Suspension without pay (for a period of one to twenty working days)
* Withholding of an annual increment
* Dismissal

It's also worth noting that discipline is only imposed ""for cause"" and must be just and reasonable, commensurate with the offense.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.0795,3.0226,134.6615,4614.0,387.3,,,,bridge
