(c) Where a full-time member is absent due to legitimate illness, the member may draw sick credits from the bank to the
extent of the member’s accumulated cred","Unfortunately, the provided text does not explicitly mention a specific duration for an illness. However, it does provide information on the expected duration of an absence and the prognosis provided in the original certificate.

In section 18.03(c), it states:

""...unless the expected duration of the absence is extended beyond the prognosis provided in the original medical certificate...""

This suggests that if the expected duration of an absence exceeds the prognosis, additional documentation or medical certificates may be required. However, no specific duration for the illness itself is defined.

If you're looking for more information on the duration of an illness, I recommend consulting other sections of the Collective Agreement or seeking clarification from a representative of the Laurentian University Faculty Association.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.7264,3.1574,27.0312,4616.0,386.4,,,,bridge
test_en_053,How does the agreement define or describe academic workload?,1f2116a0-47b6-4798-b700-28ba59302edb,0.4609,0.4494,0.0164,"ARTICLE 5.40 – ACADEMIC WORKLOAD
5.40.1 The academic workload shall be assigned in a fair and equitable manner. To help ensure this goal, each
Member of a Department/School shall receive a copy of the Chair's/Director’s recommendations to the
Dean/University Librarian on the Member's own workload and a summary of the recommendations on all
other Members in the Department/School, including any recommendations for overloads, prior to the
recommendations being forwarded to the Dean/University Libra",4ffc4230-dfa4-403f-93dd-9897712979f4,0.0164,0.0123,0.0164,"ARTICLE 10 — CORRESPONDENCE
10.01 All correspondence between the Parties described in this Agreement shall be in writing, and
to the persons named as correspondents by the Parties.
