your first (1st) year (if applicable).
12. PHYSICAL AND MENTAL ILLNESS. You are eligible for sick leave up to a maximum of six (6) months at full
salary from the date of disabil",528bb61e-3fff-4c73-b5a8-7a9319f8713f,0.4349,0.3805,0.0159,"11.23 Each offer ofappointment shall specify the course number(s), the number of credits, terms and conditions of
employment including salary, and will reference individuals to the collective agreement for benefits, professional
development funds, establishment/seniority, deemed hours and cancellation conditions. A link ofthe current collective
agreement shall be sent with every offer ofemployment.","The Collective Agreement provides various provisions related to professional development. 

According to Article 10.40, the parties agree that the University is best served when staff have opportunities for personal development and career advancement. This includes:

* $500 in expenditures per contractual year to support the activities of full-time Counsellors (Article 10.40.2)
* Professional Development Days: Full-time Professional Staff are entitled to three (3) professional development days, with requests that must be made at least seven (7) days in advance and approval not unreasonably withheld (Article 10.40.4). Part-time Clinicians receive the amount of professional development specified in Article 4.70 for each academic term of employment, with carry-forward and transfer rights outlined in Article 4.35.
* Reimbursement of tuition for full-time Professional Staff to enroll in courses/conferences outside the University (Article 10.40.5)
* An annual report is required from part-time Clinicians within 30 days of completion of their contract, which provides a broad and general overview of clinical services provided during employment (Article 10.45)

Additionally, Article 10.55 outlines salary increases for Full-Time Counsellors, including:

* A base salary minimum and CDI breakpoint
* Starting salaries reflecting qualifications and relevant work experience
* Career Development Increments, with an increase of 2.3% annually

These provisions demonstrate the collective agreement's commitment to supporting staff professional development and career advancement opportunities.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.7636,2.7406,229.0269,4614.0,393.4,,,,bridge
