(g) Upon request by the Union, the Faculty Affairs
Committee shall meet with the Union President prior to its first meeting ofthe Academic year to provide an opportunity for
the Union President to express the
Union’s opinion on the various processes i","Unfortunately, I couldn't find a specific definition of ""recommendation"" in the provided context. However, based on the Collective Agreement 2015-2018 (Article 20.04), it appears that a ""recommendation"" refers to the final decision made by the President after reviewing the recommendation from the Faculty Affairs Committee.

According to Article 20.04 (d), when the President reviews and considers the recommendation of the Faculty Affairs Committee, they shall make a final decision referencing relevant articles of Article 10. When the decision involves accepting a positive recommendation, the increment shall be applied retroactively to July 1st.

In other words, a ""recommendation"" in this context refers to the committee's final assessment and recommendation regarding a faculty member's performance, which is then considered by the President for a final decision.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,1.9613,2.3188,110.5566,4614.0,340.6,,,,bridge
