manner to give better access to funding and research collaboration at the national and international level, while promoting
research activities and creativity at Laurentian University.
6.15.2 For internally or externally-funded grant applications requesting a pre-selection or an evaluation, the
Employer shall communicate the composition of the selection committee on the RCD Office website. The participation of Faculty Members in the sele","The Collective Agreement 2011-14 and 2017-2020 states that the Employer shall provide to the Director Research, Development and Creativity a research fund to enhance scholarly productivity through an open competition among Members.

Specific details are as follows:

* For each of the years of the Collective Agreement, the Employer shall provide to the Director Research, Development and Creativity a research fund to enhance scholarly productivity through an open competition among Members: Research Support (LURF) as follows:
 + $160,000 per year
* In the event that faculty from federated or affiliated universities wish to apply, their applications shall only be considered if their home institution has contributed to the LURF fund an amount per full-time member equivalent to that provided by the Employer.
* For each of the years of the Collective Agreement, the Employer will provide to the Director Research, Development and Creativity an additional $20,000 per year to support both research activities and attendance at academic and professional conferences by retired Members, through an open competition. The Employer will also provide active assistance to LUFA-R members making grant applications to NSERC, SSHRC, and CHIR.
* A LURF Committee of eight (8) full-time Members, one (1) from Humanities, one (1) from Social Sciences, two (2) from Professional Schools, two (2) from Sciences and Engineering, one (1) from Management and one (1) Librarian will evaluate the proposals submitted to the Research, Creativity and Development (RCD) Office once a year.

It's also worth noting that previous Collective Agreements (2008-11) have slightly different details regarding LURF:

* The Employer shall provide to the Associate Vice-President, Research a research fund to enhance scholarly productivity through an open competition among Members: Research Support (LURF) as follows:
 + $140,000 per year in 2008-09
 + $150,000 per year in 2009-10
 + $160,000 per year in 2010-11
* In the event that faculty from federated or affiliated universities wish to apply, their applications shall only be considered if their home institution has contributed to the LURF fund an amount per full-time member equivalent to that provided by the Employer.
* For each of the years of the Collective Agreement, the Employer will provide to the Associate Vice-President, Research an additional $20,000 per year to support both research activities and attendance at academic and professional conferences by retired Members, through an open competition. The Employer will also provide active assistance to LUFA-R members making grant applications to NSERC, SSHRC, and CHIR.
* A LURF Committee of eight (8) full-time Members, one (1) from Humanities, one (1) from Social Sciences, two (2) from Professional Schools, two (2) from Sciences and Engineering, one (1) from Management and one (1) Librarian will evaluate the proposals submitted to the Research, Creativity and Development (RCD) Office once a year.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.1512,2.698,411.1095,4614.0,339.1,,,,bridge
