In ma","According to the context, the following conditions apply to the selection of chairs/directors:

1. The Chair of the Selection Committee must report the results of the selection process and its recommendation to the Dean/University Librarian (9.15.9).
2. If the Dean/University Librarian is prepared to accept the Selection Committee's recommendation, then they will forward this recommendation together with their own to the Vice-President, Academic, who will make the appointment (9.15.10).
3. Any outside appointment shall be made in accordance with Article 5.20 – Appointment and Renewal (9.15.12).
4. In exceptional circumstances, the Vice-President, Academic, Provost, and Dean/University Librarian may appoint an acting Chair/Director for a period of up to four months, consistent with Articles 9.20 – Term of Office of Chairs/Directors and 9.30 – Removal from Office of Chairs/Directors (9.15.13).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.0116,3.0718,29.3805,4614.0,338.2,,,,bridge
