DISMEMBERMENT. You will be required to join the life",a3289f55-009a-43a5-809f-93e00ac54102,0.4319,0.3779,0.0159,"16.03 Members shall receive designated holidays offfrom work without any loss of regular earnings.
ARTICLE 17-VACATION
17.01 Full-time members are entitled to vacation on the following basis:
(a) Members with less than one year ofservice shall receive vacation on the basis set out in the
Employment Standards Act;
(b) A member who has completed one year of continuous service as of30 June in any year shall receive vacation in the
twelve months foliowing of one month or 23 working days;
(c) A membe","According to the collective agreement, here are the rules concerning vacation:

* Members are required to take their entitled vacation (Article 17.03).
* Vacation may not be accumulated from year to year (Article 17.03).
* Members will continue to receive their normal earnings during vacation periods (Article 17.04).
* There shall be no remuneration in lieu of vacation if a member chooses not to take their vacation entitlement (Article 17.04).

Additionally, the number of days of vacation entitled to full-time members is as follows:

* Less than one year of service: based on the Employment Standards Act
* One year or more of continuous service (as of June 30 in any year): 23 working days in the following 12 months (Article 17.01(b)).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.1116,2.7461,24.4134,4616.0,344.6,,,,bridge
