President, Academic and Provost and the
Dean/University Librarian, after consultation with a Departme","According to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement, the selection of Chairs/Directors shall be conducted through an Abbreviated Selection Process. This process involves:

* The ballots being opened and counted in the presence of the Selection Committee (Article 9.15.3)
* The Chair of the Selection Committee reporting the results of the selection process and its recommendation to the Dean/University Librarian (Article 9.15.9)
* If the Dean/University Librarian is prepared to accept the Selection Committee's recommendation, the Dean/University Librarian will forward this recommendation together with their own to the Vice-President, Academic and Provost for appointment (Article 9.15.10)

If there is disagreement between the Dean/University Librarian and the Selection Committee on an appointment, the selection procedure shall be reinstated as in Article 9.15.3 above.

It's also stated that the Chair/Director must be a tenured or probationary Member of faculty (Article 9.15.12).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.7031,2.9206,30.7583,4616.0,353.5,,,,bridge
