Copyright shall be handled in accordance with the following procedure:
(a) The Member, within three (3) weeks of the eve","Patents are addressed in the collective agreement through various articles, but the main provisions can be found in Article 6.30 - Patents and Article 6.40 - Committee on Patents and Copyright.

According to Article 6.30, no patent or copyright shall be granted by the University that would infringe upon a faculty member's rights as a creator of works (Article 6.30.1).

Additionally, the Collective Bargaining Parties agree to consider recommendations regarding patents and copyrights during negotiations (Article 6.40.1).

The Committee on Patents and Copyright is established to handle grievances related to patents and copyrights, including mediation of disputes under Articles 6.30 and 6.35 (Article 6.40.3). 

