(b) Sessional rates (for other than distance education courses) for membe","The Collective Agreement 2017-2020 outlines several provisions related to distance courses. Here are the key points:

* Development of a course is considered twice the credit value of the course.
* Revision or supervision of a distance education course is considered equivalent to the credit value of the course if it's part of a full-time member's normal workload assignment. Otherwise, it's an overload payment based on the equivalence set out above.
* Sessional appointees are compensated a minimum of $1000 or at the rate of $240 (2015), $246 (2016), and $250 (2017) per half course (3 credits).
* For online courses where the core course material and activities are mediated through a web-based learning management system, and students regularly interact with each other and/or the instructor online, the Employer pays 10% more than is paid for the regular distance course.

Additionally, Article 28.01 states that teaching of a distance-education course as part of a full-time member's normal workload assignment is equivalent to the credit value of the course. Full-Time Members may only teach three (3) credits of distance education in their normal workload.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.051,3.0883,138.7652,4658.0,353.4,,,,bridge
