banned for use in subsequent proceedings as in clauses 5.70.5 to
5.70.9 below but which the University requires for matters other than those related to this Collective
Agreement.
5.70.2 Members shall have the right to examine all of their personnel files during normal business hours, after notice in
writing, in the presence of the
Dean/University Librarian or a person authorised by the Dean/University Librarian. Material in the files which is ","According to Article 5.70, Members have the right to examine their active and archival personnel files during normal business hours, after notice in writing, in the presence of the Dean/University Librarian or a person authorized by them.

Active files will contain only information allowed under this Collective Agreement, while Archival files will contain material banned for use in subsequent proceedings but required for matters other than those related to this Collective Agreement.

Members can request one copy of their personnel file (excluding confidential material) from the Vice-President, Academic, which will be provided within five working days at no charge. They can also request additional copies under the same conditions and terms.

Additionally, Members have the right to:

* Have all of their files supplemented or corrected in the event of error or inadequacy
* Request the removal of false, irrelevant, or unsubstantiated material from their personnel file
* Receive an inventory of confidential material in their file, certified by the Dean/University Librarian

Statistical summaries of student evaluations or written comments unrelated to Senate-sanctioned course evaluations will not be considered anonymous or confidential and will remain available when required.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.6376,3.034,155.8693,4659.0,351.9,,,,bridge
