1984. The onus shall be on the Member to establish her/his years of seniority prior to the a",899b2ab9-ec3e-4459-ac89-777602721004,0.4069,0.3967,0.0159,"If they are parties are unsuccessful in agreeing
upon such a chairpersonan Arbitrator within a period of twenty (20)
working days of the appointment of the second nominee, they shall request
the Minister of Labour for Ontario to appoint a chairperson an Arbitrator. The time limits specified in this Article may be extended by mutual
agreement by the Parties. However, the thirty (30) working day time limit set
out in Article11.15.1 (a) above referring a grievance to arbitration shall not
be waived","According to Article 11.15, the arbitration procedure is as follows:

* If the Parties are unsuccessful in agreeing on an arbitrator within a period of 20 working days of the appointment of the second nominee, they shall request the Minister of Labour for Ontario to appoint a chairperson and arbitrator.
* The time limits specified in this Article may be extended by mutual agreement between the Parties.
* However, the 30-working day time limit set out in Article 11.15.1 (a) above referring a grievance to arbitration shall not be waived and/or extended pursuant to the Labour Relations Act, 1995.
* Saturdays, Sundays, and Recognized and other Holidays identified in Article 7.10 – Recognized and Other Holidays are not counted in the time limits set out in this Article.
* No person may be appointed to the Arbitration Board who has been involved in an attempt to negotiate or settle the grievance.
* The Arbitration Board's arbitrator shall not be authorized to make any decisions inconsistent with the provisions of this Collective Agreement, nor to alter, modify, add to, or amend any part of this Collective Agreement.
* No matter may be submitted to arbitration which has not been properly carried through all requisite steps of the Grievance Procedure hereinbefore set out unless otherwise agreed to in writing between the Parties.
* The proceedings of the Arbitration Board shall be expedited by the Parties hereto, and the decision of the Arbitrator (majority and chairperson) will be final and binding upon the Parties hereto, and the Employee or Employees concerned.

Additionally, the Parties may mutually agree, in writing, to substitute a mutually agreeable arbitrator for the Arbitration Board at the time of reference to arbitration, and the other provisions referring to the Arbitration Board shall appropriately apply.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.0793,2.7505,144.1494,4661.0,356.7,,,,bridge
test_en_135,How does the agreement define or describe purpose of the?,61e470ca-8d46-4082-b958-76bd245c03be,0.4093,0.399,0.0164,"Hereinafter, this title shall
