Librarian/Archivist).
5.20.6 Appointments shall be made onl","According to Article 5.20 of the Collective Agreement, appointments are defined as follows:

* Appointments shall be made only to the ranks referred to in this Collective Agreement, viz, Lecturer, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Full Professor, and the corresponding library ranks (General Librarian/Archivist, Assistant Librarian/Archivist, Associate Librarian/Archivist, Full Librarian/Archivist). (Source: Article 5.20.5)

Additionally, it states that term appointments shall be limited to a total of three (3) years, except by agreement of the Parties. In cases where the limited term appointment is a replacement for an academic administrator, the appointment may be for a term up to five (5). (Source: Article 5.20.15)

Regarding renewal, it does not explicitly state the procedure for renewal, but it mentions that if a Member is reappointed, they may also apply for a promotion as per Article 5.65 - Promotion Procedures.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.0721,2.9786,30.8913,4663.0,359.6,,,,bridge
test_en_139,What are the rules concerning sabbatical leaves?,315cdcf6-c4a0-4784-8619-b8ce4f3509bb,0.4978,0.4854,0.0299,"In the event that the
Member wishes to amend the sabbatical plan, the provisions of Article 7.25.3 (f) above shall apply.
7.25.11 Sabbatical Leave After Three Years
While sabbaticals after six (6) years are the norm, the Parties recognize that outside of the sabbatical
eligibility plan, which will take precedence, it may be mutually beneficial to Members and the University if
Members were to take a six (6) month sabbatical at eighty-five percent (85%) salary after three (3) years of
service. For",df4913d4-0e4a-4457-850d-5898735d6a0e,0.4905,0.3066,0.0278,"When Members take a sabbatical leave after three
(3) years all accumulated years of eligibility are exhausted except as otherwise provided for by this
Collective Agreement. When the sabbatical leave is postponed, the Member shall receive one (1) year sabbatical credit
for the year postponed so that their next sabbatical leave will occur according to their original sabbatical rotation. Sabbaticals after three
(3) years can be granted provided that:
Eligibility
(a) Members have tenure when the lea",25a5e891-ea30-4bfd-a2ff-23f6fd6a6660,0.4905,0.3066,0.0274,"When Members take a sabbatical leave after three
(3) years all accumulated years of eligibility are exhausted except as otherwise provided for by this
Collective Agreement. When the sabbatical leave is postponed, the Member shall receive one (1) year sabbatical credit
for the year postponed so that their next sabbatical leave will occur according to their original sabbatical rotation. Sabbaticals after three
(3) years can be granted provided that:
Eligibility
(a) Members have tenure when the lea",ae9c1c14-2232-47c4-8646-7a83264fbcd5,0.5178,0.4401,0.0164,"22.09 Compensation for sabbatical leaves coincides with the Collective Agreement in place. Salary,
benefits and other provisions will be adjusted according to any new agreement between the
Board and the Association
LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020 33
<<>>",428f470f-261d-42e1-9fc3-6ff207bbff68,0.0164,0.0127,0.0164,"In the event that the Member wishes to amend the sabbatical
plan the provisions of Article 5.20.5 d shall apply.
5.20.15 Sabbatical after Three Years of Service
The parties recognize that sabbaticals after six (6) years are the norm and that the sabbatical
eligibility plan will take precedence. However, it may be mutually beneficial to Members
and the University if Members were to take a six month sabbatical at eighty-five percent
(85%) salary after three (3) years of service. For each six (6) m","According to the provided text from the Collective Agreement 2008-11 (Article 7.25 and 5.20):

1. Sabbaticals after three years can be granted, but only under specific conditions:
	* The member must have tenure when the leave becomes effective.
	* The leave does not require the postponement of a sabbatical leave for a member with six or more years of service.
	* The leave does not have a negative impact on the budget of the Department/School.
2. Sabbaticals after three years can be taken at 85% salary, but for each six months of service beyond three years, the member is eligible for an additional 2.5% of salary during the leave period.
3. When members take a sabbatical leave after three years, all accumulated years of eligibility are exhausted except as otherwise provided in this Collective Agreement.
4. If a sabbatical leave is postponed, the member receives one year's sabbatical credit for the year postponed, so that their next sabbatical leave occurs according to their original rotation.
5. Members must prepare and forward a full written account of their scholarly and professional activities and accomplishments within one month of their return from the leave.

Additionally, the text also mentions Study Leaves (Article 7.30 and 5.25), which are available to tenured, tenure-track, or permanent sessional members after two years of full-time service, but only upon approval by the Provost after consultation with the Department and following an approved application procedure.

It's worth noting that there is also a separate provision regarding compensation for sabbatical leaves (Article 22.09), which states that salary, benefits, and other provisions will be adjusted according to any new agreement between the Board and the Association.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.6545,2.6309,289.7076,4665.0,365.1,,,,bridge
