on campus are entitled to suitable office space on campus. Sabbaticants required to mov",52fc4325-4b55-4a94-ac1a-817eaae394c9,0.5478,0.3834,0.0313,"Members who are on sabbatical leave and who elect to remain on campus for all or part of the duration of the leave shall
not normally be assigned any formal workload nor shall they normally participate in any formal activities of the University
other than those required by this Collective
Agreement. Members who have indicated in their sabbatical plan their intent to spend part or all of their sabbatical leave
on campus are entitled to suitable office space on campus. Sabbaticants required to mov",f8b3f82f-eddb-46a6-9756-262dc7f291bc,0.5227,0.4443,0.031,"Members who are on sabbatical leave and who elect to remain on campus for all or part of the duration of the leave shall
not normally be assigned any formal workload nor shall they normally participate in any formal activities of the University
other than those required by this Collective Agreement. Members who have indicated in their sabbatical plan their intent to spend part or all of their sabbatical leave on campus
are entitled to suitable office space on campus. Sabbaticants required to mov","According to Article 7.25 of the Collective Agreement, members who are on sabbatical leave and elect to remain on campus for all or part of the duration of the leave are not normally assigned any formal workload nor participate in formal university activities other than those required by this Collective Agreement.

Members who have indicated in their sabbatical plan their intent to spend part or all of their sabbatical leave on campus are entitled to suitable office space on campus. Sabbaticants required to move their offices shall have all moving and storage expenses paid by the Employer. The Employer will replace Members on sabbatical leave when it deems necessary.

Additionally, eligibility for sabbatical leave is subject to certain conditions:

* Members must have been full-time faculty members of the University for at least 6 consecutive years.
* They must be tenured at the time their sabbatical leave begins (except in exceptional circumstances).
* The leave can be granted for a maximum of 6 months at a time, with a maximum of 2.5% additional salary per 6 months after 3 years of service.

It's also worth noting that sabbaticals after 3 years are not automatically postponed, but rather are subject to the provisions outlined in Article 7.25.11, which include providing one year of sabbatical credit if a leave is postponed and requiring the member to return to the University for at least 6 months after completing their leave.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,1.9922,3.5897,310.6679,4665.0,366.9,,,,bridge
test_en_145,How does the agreement define or describe compassionate leave?,ae77f0ab-a846-4d20-9ce3-ac2edb34ad07,0.3953,0.336,0.0311,"24.04 Bereavement/Compassionate
In the event of the death of a Member of a Member's family, the Member shall be granted a
leave of absence of at least seven (7) working days without loss of pay. If more than seven
days is requested, the President shall decide the maximum number of leave days granted to
qualify for this leave.
The term “Member ofa Member's family” means
Spouse (which includes common-law spouse and same-sex)
Child (which includes step-child)
Sibling (includes step-sibling)
Parent ",1b4b2aff-dfea-4654-8537-4a7efc2a18be,0.3778,0.3022,0.0301,"14.07 Compassionate Leave
A full-time Member, who holds a tenured or probationary appointment within the University, shall be eligible for a paid
leave of absence for a period of up a maximum of 3 days per calendar year to fulfill responsibilities relating to the special
needs of a member of the Employee's family.
Special needs may include, but are not restricted to, resettlement of aged or disabled parents, serious illness of parents,
partner, or child, medical treatment of partner or child tha",f3441039-61a7-486d-8ae9-ac86636fb387,0.3778,0.3022,0.0297,"14.07 Compassionate Leave
A full-time Member, who holds a tenured or probationary appointment within the University, shall be eligible for a paid
leave of absence for a period of up a maximum of 3 days per calendar year to fulfill responsibilities relating to the special
needs of a member of the Employee's family.
Special needs may include, but are not restricted to, resettlement of aged or disabled parents, serious illness of parents,
