requ","According to Section 5.90.3 of the Collective Agreement 2011-14 (page number not specified, as it is not included in the provided text snippet), there is no mention of employer's retirement being explicitly stated.

However, it can be inferred that the collective agreement addresses the issue of pension portability for members who are hired after a certain date and are eligible to receive an early retirement incentive. According to Section 5.90.3, proposed members hired after September 24, 2017, will not have the option to commute the value of their pension benefit upon retirement or resignation.

It's also worth noting that Section 212 of the Collective Agreement 2011-14 mentions the allowable roll-over amount and how it is spread over the years of the Special Voluntary Early Retirement. This section does not explicitly address employer's retirement, but rather focuses on the member's retirement benefits.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.0563,3.3132,30.854,4667.0,362.2,,,,bridge
