7.35.1 The Employer and the Union endorse the principle of voluntary reduced workload as being mutua","According to Article 7.35 of the Collective Agreement 2017-2020, the employer and the union (Laurentian University Faculty Association) endorse the principle of voluntary reduced workload as being mutually beneficial to both members and the institution.

Specifically, the agreement states that any full-time member of the bargaining unit who currently occupies a regular full-time position and has a minimum of two years of continuous full-time service at the university can be granted up to 50% temporary reduction in workload with a proportionate reduction in pay (Article 7.35.1).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.0486,3.1466,20.8502,4669.0,364.1,,,,bridge
