normal vacation entitlement set out above.",c12267f4-ef9b-4ec0-848b-f2e1ec639626,0.4032,0.3528,0.0164,"17.03 Members are required to take the vacation to which they are entitled. Vacation may not be accumulated from year
to year.
17.04 Members will continue to receive their normal earnings during vacation periods, but there shall be no remuneration
in lieu ofvacation in the event that a member chooses not to take the vacation entitlement.",33f8516e-e862-4def-832f-3ecd8cbd0374,0.0164,0.0127,0.0164,"ARTICLE 5.15 – VACATION
5.15.1 Nine (9) Months or More of Continuous Service
Every Member who has completed nine (9) months or more of continuous service with the
Employer by May 31 in any academic year shall be entitled to be absent from work during
one (1) month or twenty-five (25) working days in each year following such May 31.
5.15.2 Sixty (60) Months or More of Continuous Service
Every Member who has completed sixty (60) months or more of continuous service with
the Employer by May 31 in a","According to Article 5.15 of the collective agreement, several conditions apply to vacation:

1. Members are required to take the vacation to which they are entitled (Article 5.15.6a).
2. Vacation may not be accumulated from year to year (Article 5.15.6a).
3. Members must take their annual vacation between June 1 and Labour Day, unless prior permission has been granted by the President (Article 5.15.6b.1). 
4. If members are unable to complete scheduled duties assigned to them before annual vacation, they must report to the President at least one month in advance of the dates of their intended vacation (Article 5.15.6b.2).

Additionally, there is also a clause regarding payment in lieu of vacation:

* Members will be paid during vacation periods, but there shall be no remuneration in lieu of vacation in the event that a member chooses not to take her/his vacation allowance (Article 5.15.4 and 17.04).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.2401,2.7419,79.823,4671.0,366.2,,,,bridge
