$40,000. Time spent on any other type of leave with a period of more than six (6) months,
including LTD leave, shall not count toward the eligibility requirements of three (3) years of
uninterrupted service, nor toward years of service for the purpose of determining salary
while on study leave.
LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020 34
<<>>","Study leaves are addressed in Article 7.30 of the LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020. According to this article, a study leave is a type of leave granted for the purpose of upgrading academic qualifications, normally through the attainment of a higher degree or some other equivalent acceptable to the University and the Department/School.

The key points regarding study leaves are:

* The maximum length of study leaves granted during a Member's academic career shall not exceed two (2) years.
* A study leave may be granted to a tenured, probationary, or untenured faculty member, as stated in Article 7.30.1 Eligibility.

Additionally, the collective agreement outlines the compensation for members on study leave: they shall receive 30% of their salary to a maximum of $40,000.

It's worth noting that time spent on other types of leave with a period of more than six (6) months will not count towards the eligibility requirements or years of service.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.6378,2.9033,31.1183,4671.0,365.3,,,,bridge
