Collective Agreement 2008-11
CLARITY NOTE:
For the purposes of clarity, the parties agree that the bargaining unit does not include full-time faculty on reduced
assignments, persons employed through the
Centre for Continuing Education, persons employed to teach courses primarily for students who are not registered in a
degree credit programme, persons not assigned responsibili","Laurentian University Research is addressed in several sections of the Collective Agreement:

* Article 6.20 - RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT SUPPORT
* Article 6.25 - LAURENTIAN UNIVERSITY RESEARCH FUND (LURF)

Under these articles, the Employer is responsible for providing various forms of support to promote research activities and creativity at Laurentian University, including:

* A research fund (LURF) that provides $160,000 per year to enhance scholarly productivity through an open competition among Members
* An additional $20,000 per year to support both research activities and attendance at academic and professional conferences by retired Members, Sessional Members, and Master Lecturers
* Active assistance to these Members making grant applications to NSERC, SSHRC, and CIHR

Additionally, the Collective Agreement also addresses the following research-related matters:

* The provision of resources to assist all Members in preparing grant applications (Article 6.15)
* The communication of the composition and terms of reference of selection committees for internal or externally-funded grant applications (Article 6.15.1)
* The Start-up Grant of $8,000 provided to new full-time Members with probationary or tenured appointments (Article 6.20.1)",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.1493,3.1512,353.1425,4669.0,371.7,,,,bridge
