<<>>",c7440c4f-ecd9-4e32-b645-e4abf25fb24d,0.3901,0.3413,0.0159,"2.04 Both the French and the English versions ofthe collective agreement shall be the official and definitive versions.
Both parties may use either the English or the French version in any proceedings arising out ofthe collective agreement,
and shall apply the version ofthe collective agreement in which formal grievance/arbitration proceedings were initiated.","According to Article 2 - LANGUAGES, the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement defines languages as follows:

* The University is committed to the fulfilment of its role as a bilingual and tri-cultural institution of higher learning. (ARTICLE 2 - LANGUAGES, 2.01)
* The Employer and the Union pledge themselves to the maintenance and promotion of English and French languages, as well as the revitalization of Indigenous languages. (ARTICLE 2 - LANGUAGES, 2.01)

Additionally, Section 39.02 states that the Committee shall define intellectual patents and copyright, but it does not specifically describe or define languages.

It's worth noting that the agreement also states that both the French and English versions of the collective agreement are official and definitive versions (ARTICLE 2 - LANGUAGES, 2.04), and that either version can be used in any proceedings arising out of the collective agreement.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.7899,2.6315,30.1256,4669.0,371.8,,,,bridge
