<<>>",ebfc7453-86f6-41d8-8af7-c7ea61a59bf7,0.3341,0.2923,0.0159,"ARTICLE 1 - PURPOSE AND DEFINITIONS
1.01 It is the purpose ofthis Collective Agreement to set forth the terms and conditions ofemployment and other specific
contractual provisions, to promote and maintain harmonious relationships between the Parties, to facilitate the Parties in
working together to encourage the development ofresearch and teaching necessary for the provision ofhigh quality
education to students, and to provide a means for settling such disputes as may arise from time to time.","According to Article 5 - MANAGEMENT RIGHTS, specifically Section 5.01, the agreement states that:

""The Association recognizes that the Employer has retained and shall possess and exercise all rights and functions,
powers, privileges and authority that the Employer possessed prior to the signing of this Agreement with the
Association, excepting those that are clearly and specifically relinquished or restricted in this Agreement, or modified by
statute.""

This means that the Employer retains and exercises all its pre-existing rights, powers, privileges, and authority, except for those explicitly relinquished or restricted in the agreement.

Additionally, Section 39.02 and 40.02 of the same article mention the Intellectual Property Committee, which is responsible for defining intellectual patents and copyright (Section 39.02, part a), conducting business related to it, considering strategies for marketing inventions, improvements, or discoveries, and recommending modifications to the patents and copyright articles (Section 40.02, parts c and d).

Let me know if you have any further questions!",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.0903,2.3112,32.0116,4671.0,371.8,,,,bridge
