(b) The following documents will be required to request payment of the insurance carrier:
(i) The beneficiary must complete a Statement required by the insurance carrier as well as
provide her/his Social ","According to Article 16 of the collective agreement:

* During the Voluntary Early Retirement period, benefits will apply as follows:
 + Members considered to be on leave with pay will retain participation in certain plans (Group Life Insurance, Dependent Group Life, Accidental Death and Dismemberment, Hospital Care, Extended Medical, and the Retirees Health Benefit Plan).
 + Members no longer considered employees may choose to retain participation in these plans.
 
Additionally, Article 8.80.3 states that if a Member dies prior to receiving a pension, the following conditions apply:

* The University shall contact the Beneficiary and outline the procedures to be followed.
* The Beneficiary must complete an ""Application for Death Benefit"".
* Provide a Death Certificate.
* Provide a ""notarial copy"" of the Employee's ""Last Will and Testament"".
* All Members should have a current ""Last Will and Testament"".
* Beneficiaries of Members without a ""Last Will and Testament"" will have to settle any disputes between potential Beneficiaries (children vs spouse) in the courts, prior to receiving any funds from the Pension Plan.

There is also an article stating that if within seven days the University has not been contacted by the beneficiary, the University shall make every reasonable effort to contact the beneficiary.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.0659,2.5126,250.0356,4669.0,372.9,,,,bridge
