for the year postponed so that their next sabbatical leave will occur according to their original sabbatical rotation. Sabbaticals after three
(3) years can be granted provided that:
Eligibility
(a) Members have tenure when the lea",d7575fdd-8f59-49a4-b6ce-5bec4bc801a9,0.502,0.4016,0.0159,"12.20 Immediately following the completion of a sabbatical leave, the member is required to return to the University for a
period equal to the length of the leave taken, or to satisfy some other arrangement that is mutually acceptable to the
member and the Employer.","According to the Collective Agreement, the rules concerning sabbatical leaves are as follows:

* A sabbatical leave can be for 12 months or 6 months, with the option of starting on July 1st or January 1st. (Article 22.07)
* The duration of a sabbatical leave does not count towards years of eligibility, but the member is still entitled to vacation pay proportional to the length of the leave. (Article 22.07)
* Members who terminate their employment between June 1 and Labour Day with no formal teaching duties during that period are deemed to have taken as much of their vacation entitlement as possible during that time. (Article 5.20)
* When a member takes a sabbatical leave after three years, all accumulated years of eligibility are exhausted except for the year(s) already used towards the eligibility requirement. (Article 22.07)
* If a sabbatical leave is postponed, the member receives one year of sabbatical credit to maintain their original sabbatical rotation schedule.
* When a member completes a sabbatical leave, they are required to return to the University for a period equal to the length of the leave taken, or participate in an alternative arrangement mutually agreed upon by the member and the Employer. (Article 12.20)

It's also worth noting that during their sabbatical leave, members are covered for:

* Sick leave up to the extent of their actual salary paid during that period (Article 7.55)
* Long-term disability coverage
* Pension plan contributions based on their actual salary
* Life insurance coverage based on their actual salary

However, it's also important to clarify that specific details about long-term disability coverage should be provided to members at the time of appointment (Article 22.07(e)).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.5609,2.7013,51.5326,4669.0,376.6,,,,bridge
