satisfactory performance.","According to Article 11.10 of the Collective Agreement, a ""redundancy"" refers to a specific type of dismissal that is subject to the procedures outlined in this article.

Specifically, Section 11.10 states that no other procedures will be used to deal with redundancies as defined in Article 11.10.3. Additionally, it is understood that the term ""redundancy"" does not apply to limited-term appointments (as per Article 5.20).

It's also worth noting that a ""workload redundancy"" (defined in Section 11.10) is a specific type of redundancy where a program is eliminated due to insufficient academic personnel, as long as the Employer can demonstrate that the proposed reductions are consistent with normal workloads.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.112,2.907,30.3541,4671.0,374.4,,,,bridge
