contractual provisions, to promote and maintain harmonious relationships between the Parties, to facilitate the Parties in
working together to encourage the development ofresearch and teaching necessary for the provision ofhigh quality
education to students, and to provide a means for settling such disputes as may arise from time to time.","The Collective Agreement states that specific scholarly tasks other than teaching/professional librarianship duties shall not be imposed by the Dean/University Librarian, except for the appointment of an Acting Chair/Director as per Articles 9.15 and 9.20.

Article 5.40.6(a) specifically mentions this condition: ""The Dean/University Librarian, in accordance with Article 3.10 – Academic Freedom, shall not impose specific scholarly tasks other than the teaching/professional librarianship duties referred to in Article 5.40.5 above.""

This means that employees are protected from having excessive workload or being assigned specific tasks that compromise their academic freedom unless it is related to internal governance of the department/school, appointment of an Acting Chair/Director, or a university-related community activity.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.6569,3.0493,109.5709,4669.0,374.6,,,,bridge
