test_en_243,What does the collective agreement provide regarding discipline?,189ba770-955f-4d0a-be39-0b169dd5d120,0.4219,0.4113,0.0328,"Discipline shall be just and reasonable,
based on the principle of progressive discipline, except in egregious cases.
5.75.2 Just cause shall be defined as:
(a) Gross misconduct including serious unprofessional behaviour and/or misconduct constituting a grave
and direct violation of the personal safety of another Member; Members of the University community
and/or students of the University community.
(b) Persistent failure to discharge academic responsibility as defined in this Collective Agreem",4a4c295b-8cd0-4342-aa27-1ce920bf3844,0.4342,0.304,0.0308,"The Member and her/his union representative shall be given five (5) working days’ notice of the time and place of the
meeting wherever possible or practicable. The Dean/University Librarian shall review with the member the particulars of the allegation with the
Member and shall provide the Member with the opportunity to respond to these allegations. The
Parties shall attempt to resolve the matter in a manner acceptable to all concerned.
5.75.6 When the Vice-President, Academic and Provost is sat",b7da3e51-5b16-4cb0-baff-e573d731b5a3,0.4262,0.2664,0.0306,"Disciplinary action shall be just and reasonable and
be commensurate with the offense.
5.75.2 ""Cause"" for disciplinary measures shall include:
(a) Serious unprofessional behaviour.
(b) Failure to comply with any of the provisions of this Collective Agreement, minor technical violations excepted.
5.75.3 The following are the only formal ""Disciplinary
Measures"" which may be taken by the Employer against a Member:
(a) A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the pe",71f4af0f-3901-4ed1-bebb-9ced7441a387,0.4342,0.304,0.0303,"The Member and her/his union representative shall be given five (5) working days’ notice of the time and place of the
meeting wherever possible or practicable. The Dean/University Librarian shall review with the member the particulars of the allegation with the
Member and shall provide the Member with the opportunity to respond to these allegations. The
Parties shall attempt to resolve the matter in a manner acceptable to all concerned.
5.75.6 When the Vice-President, Academic and Provost is sat",1879e4a0-c6c1-4ad9-b5b2-c1cb75b72da7,0.4262,0.2664,0.0301,"Disciplinary action shall be just and reasonable and
be commensurate with the offense.
5.75.2 ""Cause"" for disciplinary measures shall include:
(a) Serious unprofessional behaviour.
(b) Failure to comply with any of the provisions of this Collective Agreement, minor technical violations excepted.
5.75.3 The following are the only formal ""Disciplinary
Measures"" which may be taken by the Employer against a Member:
(a) A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the pe","According to the Collective Agreement, the following are the only forms of discipline that may be taken by the Employer against a Member:

1. A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the personnel file (5.75.3(a));
2. The withholding of an annual increment (5.75.3(b));
3. The suspension without pay; the reduction in pay shall be computed as one two hundred and sixtieth (1/260) of normal salary per day of suspension (5.75.3(c));
4. The suspension with pay; if and only if the Vice-President, Academic cites the suspension with pay as a disciplinary measure (5.75.3(d));
5. Dismissal of a Member (5.75.3(e));

Note that the Collective Agreement also provides specific procedures for investigating and imposing discipline, including notice periods, meetings with the Member and Union representative, and timelines for completing investigations and imposing discipline.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.3124,2.9224,146.6904,4671.0,308.2,,,,bridge
