9.15","The selection of Chairs/Directors is addressed in Article 9.15 of the collective agreement.

To be specific:

* The Chair/Director shall be a tenured or probationary Member of faculty (Article 9.15.12).
* In exceptional circumstances, an acting Chair/Director may be appointed for up to four months by the Vice-President, Academic and Provost, and the Dean/University Librarian, after consultation with a Department/School (Article 9.15.13).
* The ballots shall be opened and counted in the presence of the Selection Committee (Article 9.15.9).
* If the Dean/University Librarian is prepared to accept the Selection Committee's recommendation, she/he will forward this recommendation together with her/his own to the Vice-President, Academic, who will make the appointment (Article 9.15.10).

Note: There is also an abbreviated selection process mentioned in Article 9.15.14, but it seems that this section is not fully quoted in the provided context.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.3198,3.1451,31.6817,4669.0,379.5,,,,bridge
