7.25.7 Benefits
(a) During the period of sabbatical leave, the Member shall continue to receive all benefits as per Article
8.45 – Benefits subject to the conditions set out therein.
(b) During a sabbatical leave, pension calculations shall be based on the Member's salary that would
have been in effect if the Member had not been on sabbatical.
7.25","Here are the answers to your question based on the provided context:

1. The application procedure for sabbatical leave must be followed.
2. Credit towards a sabbatical leave may be granted by the Vice-President, Academic and Provost from time-to-time for full-time faculty service at another University.
3. Members can apply for sabbatical leave one (1) year prior to the year in which they would normally become eligible to take sabbatical leave under special circumstances.
4. The Dean/University Librarian may request that Members apply for their sabbatical leave after the completion of five (5) years.
5. If a Member accepts the request, they must submit a sabbatical plan by September 30 and receive a stipend of eighty-five percent (85%) of their salary during the leave.

Please let me know if you would like to ask another question or clarify any information related to sabbatical leave.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.5367,2.2223,235.8113,4669.0,386.6,,,,bridge
test_en_255,How is faculty affairs committee (fac) addressed in the collective agreement?,72dffc95-25a7-4238-9d8a-214f94243132,0.4558,0.3646,0.0318,"ARTICLE 8 – FACULTY AFFAIRS COMMITTEE (FAC)
