single letter of assessment of the Department/","According to Article 5.55.16, an applicant may ask that a Faculty Personnel Committee Member recuse themselves from a particular case on the grounds of conflict of interest or reasonable apprehension of bias. The Chair of the Committee will render a decision with reasons to the applicant and the Member in question if the Member is to be recused.

Additionally, the Committee shall consider any dispute arising out of Articles 4.71 and 4.72 in accordance with Paragraph 3 below. This includes addressing claims related to committee apprehension (Article 5.55.16) in a manner that ensures impartiality and fairness.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.742,2.9224,221.1316,4669.0,385.1,,,,bridge
test_en_274,What is stated about faculty appointments?,2270c363-4d9b-4722-af06-3548ced9c851,0.4677,0.3976,0.0164,"ARTICLE 13 — FACULTY APPOINTMENTS
13.01 The process of developing recommendations on the appointment of Faculty is a peer-review
process. The University recognizes that input from Members of the same discipline as the
contemplated appointment is important; however, it is agreed that the Employer determines
the faculty complement necessary to carry out its objectives and mission, and final decisions
are the responsibility of the Board and President.",db5a06c5-42e0-4cc2-b099-c26a09852e2c,0.0164,0.0123,0.0164,"15.02 In addition to the items set out in Article 11, Academic Activity, in conducting evaluations for
