13.01 The process of developing recommendations on the appointment of Faculty is a peer-review
process. The University recognizes that input from Members of the same discipline as the
contemplated appointment is important; however, it is agreed that the Employer determines
the faculty complement necessary to carry out its objectives and mission, and final decisions
are the responsibility of the Board and President.
LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2012-2016 17
<<>>","According to Article 13 of the LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2012-2016:

* The appointment process for Faculty is a peer-review process (Article 13.01)
* The University determines the faculty complement necessary to carry out its objectives and mission, with final decisions resting with the Board and President (Article 13.01)
* All new appointments must be advertised within and outside the University in suitable national publications (Article 13.07a)
* A search committee will be established by the department where the appointment is to be made (Article 13.07b)

It's also mentioned that during evaluations for recommending renewal of probationary appointments, the committee will review prior performance and provide formative comments on what further is required for obtaining tenure, as well as any concerns raised about satisfactory performance (Article 15.02).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.076,2.348,24.8036,4671.0,385.2,,,,bridge
