12.01 The President will assign academic workload in a fair and equitable manner. Such workload
includes, in proportions that may vary from Member to Member, and from year to year for
the same Member, the following components: teaching/librarianship, scholarly activity, and
governance and community service.","The collective agreement provides the following regarding workload:

* Academic workload includes, in proportions that may vary from Member to Member, and from year to year for the same Member, the following components:
  * Teaching/librarianship
  * Scholarly activity
  * Governance and community service (Article 12.01)
* Workload shall not be altered except in cases of emergency (5.40.7). However, alterations for reasonable program requirements and low enrolment may be made within 30 days of the start of the term.
* When an assigned course(s) is cancelled due to zero registration, there arises an obligation on the part of the Member to undertake additional work to maintain fairness and equity within the Department/School (5.40.7).
* A Member is entitled to one (1) term without scheduled teaching among the Fall, Winter, and Spring terms as part of their normal workload (5.40.8(a)).
* In the case of distance education courses or off-campus courses, consultation times shall be arranged for the teaching locale in accordance with the requirements of the subject matter (5.40.8(b)).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.6287,2.8637,219.3972,4669.0,391.5,,,,bridge
