faculty, staffand students — to express their opinions.
(e) The Employer shall not supervise or restrain, nor will it assume responsib","According to the Collective Agreement 2017-2020, Academic Freedom (Article 3.10), it includes:

1. The right to search for truth, knowledge, and understanding
2. The right to express freely what one believes
3. Freedom in teaching
4. Freedom in research and scholarship
5. Freedom to produce and perform creative works
6. Freedom to acquire, preserve, and provide access to documentary material in all formats
7. Freedom to participate in professional and representative academic bodies
8. Freedom to engage in service to the institution and the community
9. Freedom to express one's opinion about the University, its administration, and the system in which one works

However, it is also stated that Academic Freedom does not confer legal immunity (Article 3.10) nor does it diminish the obligations of members to perform satisfactorily their duties and responsibilities in their capacity as professors.

Additionally, Article 3.15 states that the Employer recognizes the need to provide an environment free from discrimination and harassment.

It is also mentioned that Academic Freedom entails the right of Members to exercise their civil liberties as individuals, including the right to contribute to social change through free expression on matters of public interest (Article 3.10(h)).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.2257,2.812,118.9154,4671.0,392.0,,,,bridge
