ARTICLE 7.35 – VOLUNTARY REDUCED WORKLOAD
7.35.1 The Employer and the Union endorse the principle of voluntary reduced workload as being mutually
beneficial to the Members ",4b062c5e-bd57-492d-a9a7-a1ce1826ce5a,0.4825,0.2292,0.0302,"Members on voluntary reduced workload may
contribute to the pension plan on the basis of their normal full salary
with appropriate contributions from the employee and employer as
outlined in the Collective Agreement to the extent possible under
