d) Life Insurance. Life insurance may be","According to Article 7.35 – VOLUNTARY REDUCED WORKLOAD, the rules regarding voluntary reduced workload are as follows:

1. Full-time members of the Bargaining Unit who have at least two years of continuous full-time service can request a temporary reduction in workload up to 50% with a proportionate reduction in pay.
2. The request must be made in writing and approved by both the Employer (Laurentian University) and the Union (Laurentian University Faculty Association).
3. The report of the reduced workload will become part of the employee's personnel file.
4. Time spent on study leave does not count towards sabbatical credit, as per Article 7.30.6.

It is also mentioned that:

* Members on voluntary reduced workload may contribute to the pension plan based on their normal full salary, with appropriate contributions from the employee and employer.
* However, contributions based on reduced salary may not be possible under Revenue Canada regulations for a cumulative total of more than five years.

Please note that life insurance benefits are also affected by the voluntary reduced workload arrangement (Article 7.35, d), but it seems this is an additional detail rather than a separate rule.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.6615,2.8461,34.8327,4671.0,389.7,,,,bridge
