maintained in accordance with this Article for any official purposes including disciplinary measures. There
shall be two (2) types of files for Members, active files and archival files. Active files shall contain only
information allowed under this Article. Archival files shall contain material which has been banned for use
in subsequent proceedings as in Articles 5.70.5 to 5.70.9 below but which the University requi",8d1d21eb-fb69-45a7-b991-20290cd53291,0.4471,0.4359,0.0288,"The Employer agrees not to use any unofficial personnel information that is not
maintained in accordance with this Article for any official purposes including disciplinary measures. There
shall be two (2) types of files for Members, active files and archival files. Active files shall contain only
information allowed under this Article. Archival files shall contain material which has been banned for use
in subsequent proceedings as in Articles 5.70.5 to 5.70.9 below but which the University requi",ef085307-02c3-4916-a284-8444e27c465c,0.0164,0.0127,0.0164,"No anonymous material concerning any Member shall be kept by the Employer for
inclusion in the Member’s personnel file. Statistical summaries of student evaluations
or written summaries of student comments unrelated to Senate sanctioned course
evaluations, such summaries to exclude anonymous comments, shall neither be
considered anonymous nor confidential and shall remain available when required by
this Agreement.
b. Members shall have the right to have all of their files supplemented or correct","According to Article 21 of the Collective Agreement 2015-2018, the following rules apply:

1. Official personnel files of a member are kept by the President and are the property of the Employer (21.01).
2. Members have the right to examine their official personnel files upon making prior arrangements to do so (21.02).
3. Material in the files that is confidential will be removed from the files before inspection by the member, except for material specifically excluded from confidentiality (21.02).
4. The Employer agrees not to use any unofficial personnel information that is not maintained in accordance with this Article for official purposes, including disciplinary measures (21.03).

Additionally, there are two types of files:

1. Active files: contain only information allowed under the Agreement.
2. Archival files: contain material banned for use in subsequent proceedings but required by the University.

Finally, no anonymous material concerning a member shall be kept by the Employer for inclusion in their personnel file (21.04). Statistical summaries of student evaluations can be used without being considered anonymous or confidential, and members have the right to have all of their files supplemented or corrected (21.04.b).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.2225,2.7696,34.215,4671.0,389.7,,,,bridge
