Collective Agreement 2017-2020 library service and learn under its auspices. They shall be free to carry out research and to publish its results, free to teach, to discuss and to criticise b","According to the Collective Agreement 2017-2020, Academic Freedom (Article 2) states that:

* Academic freedom is the right to search for truth, knowledge and understanding and to express freely what one believes.
* The University and Faculty Association as institutions and the community of their scholars have a duty to protect and defend the search for knowledge and truth by all who enquire, teach, and learn under its auspices.

In other words, academic freedom is essential to the university's teaching and research activities, and it involves the right to carry out research, publish results, teach, discuss, and criticize without restriction or fear of reprisal.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.7616,2.7531,20.9557,4671.0,388.8,,,,bridge
