1.15.2 The Parties agree to coope","According to Article 8.80 of the Collective Agreement 2017-2020, the beneficiary is required to contact the Pension and Benefits Officer in the Personnel Office within seven (7) days of the University's notification if they have not already been contacted. The University will then make every reasonable effort to contact the beneficiary.

Additionally, the following documents are required to request payment of life insurance proceeds:

* A Statement completed by the beneficiary
* Social Insurance Number
* Notice of the Employee's death from Obituary Notices
* Death Certificate
* Last insurance certificate issued to the faculty Member

The Life Insurance proceeds are usually paid within one (1) month.

If a member dies prior to receiving a pension, the following procedures apply:

* The University will contact the Beneficiary and outline the procedures to be followed.
* The Beneficiary must complete an ""Application for Death Benefit"".
* Provide a Death Certificate.
* Provide a notarial copy of the Employee's Last Will and Testament.
* All Members should have a current Last Will and Testament.
* Beneficiaries of members without a Last Will and Testament will need to settle disputes between potential beneficiaries in court prior to receiving any funds from the Pension Plan.

The death benefit from the Pension Plan is usually paid within two (2) to three (3) months.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.1625,2.8519,229.0472,4669.0,387.0,,,,bridge
