10.30.1 Clinicians
Clinicians who have received 3 contracts within a 6 year period will be deemed to have Seniority, and shall
have priority of hire over external candidates. Available contracts will first be offered to individuals with the
most years of service. Where two members have equal years of service, the member with the most
cumulative months of service be awarded the contract. Individuals who are on an approved leave will continue to accrue active service time","According to Article 10.30, the Employer's seniority obligation to a Sessional Member can be revoked by the Council. Specifically, Section 4.40.5 states:

""The Council's determination may request that the Member be cautioned or that the Employer's seniority obligation to the
Sessional Member be revoked or that the Member be placed on probation for the duration of one (1) course and that a further
determination be made at the conclusion of that course.""

No specific page number is mentioned, as this appears to be an excerpt from the collective agreement.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,3.5215,3.0198,19.8723,4671.0,387.4,,,,bridge
