the duties performed by a
Faculty Member with a full-time appointment.
(c) Cancellation prior to its commencement of a course for which con",db72481a-a6bb-4aa5-ba19-aa50bb368d7b,0.4338,0.3688,0.0159,"16.03 Members shall normally apply for their own promotion. Applications may also be submitted
by Members or by the President on behalf of Members who have not applied themselves,
where the Members have declared their willingness to be considered.
LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020 27
<<>>","Promotion procedures are addressed in Article 5.65 of the Collective Agreement.

Here are the key points:

* Members shall normally apply for their own promotion, but applications may also be submitted by Chairs/Directors or a Dean/University Librarian on behalf of members who have not applied themselves, where the member has declared their willingness to be considered (Article 16.03, LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020, page 27).
* Applications must be made on the prescribed application form and forwarded in paper and electronic form to the office of the applicant's Dean/University Librarian, together with a paper copy of all necessary and relevant documentation (Article 5.65.4).
* The application for promotion must reach the Dean/University Librarian not later than July 2 for decision in that academic year.
* Members are urged to consult with the Dean/University Librarian well in advance of the application deadline.
* If requested by June 1, the Dean/University Librarian will prepare a preliminary written assessment based on the requirements set out in Article 5.10 – Academic Qualifications Guidelines within one week of receiving the Member's application (Article 5.65.5).
* The following documents must be attached to the application for promotion: an updated curriculum vitae, and for applications for promotion to Full Professor/Librarian, a list of at least three referees and a copy of the research and creative works to be considered in the examination of the application (Article 5.65.6).
* Recommendations in promotion cases will follow the assessment procedure outlined in Article 5.50 – Assessment of a Member's Performance.

It is worth noting that Sessional Members have different promotion procedures, as addressed in Article 4.25 and 2.92 of the Collective Agreement.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.8194,2.3032,152.0089,4669.0,389.8,,,,bridge
test_en_314,What does the collective agreement provide regarding discipline?,189ba770-955f-4d0a-be39-0b169dd5d120,0.4311,0.4203,0.0315,"Discipline shall be just and reasonable,
based on the principle of progressive discipline, except in egregious cases.
5.75.2 Just cause shall be defined as:
(a) Gross misconduct including serious unprofessional behaviour and/or misconduct constituting a grave
and direct violation of the personal safety of another Member; Members of the University community
and/or students of the University community.
(b) Persistent failure to discharge academic responsibility as defined in this Collective Agreem",4a4c295b-8cd0-4342-aa27-1ce920bf3844,0.4427,0.3099,0.031,"The Member and her/his union representative shall be given five (5) working days’ notice of the time and place of the
meeting wherever possible or practicable. The Dean/University Librarian shall review with the member the particulars of the allegation with the
Member and shall provide the Member with the opportunity to respond to these allegations. The
Parties shall attempt to resolve the matter in a manner acceptable to all concerned.
5.75.6 When the Vice-President, Academic and Provost is sat",b7da3e51-5b16-4cb0-baff-e573d731b5a3,0.4508,0.2817,0.0307,"Disciplinary action shall be just and reasonable and
be commensurate with the offense.
5.75.2 ""Cause"" for disciplinary measures shall include:
(a) Serious unprofessional behaviour.
(b) Failure to comply with any of the provisions of this Collective Agreement, minor technical violations excepted.
5.75.3 The following are the only formal ""Disciplinary
Measures"" which may be taken by the Employer against a Member:
(a) A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the pe",71f4af0f-3901-4ed1-bebb-9ced7441a387,0.4427,0.3099,0.0306,"The Member and her/his union representative shall be given five (5) working days’ notice of the time and place of the
meeting wherever possible or practicable. The Dean/University Librarian shall review with the member the particulars of the allegation with the
Member and shall provide the Member with the opportunity to respond to these allegations. The
Parties shall attempt to resolve the matter in a manner acceptable to all concerned.
5.75.6 When the Vice-President, Academic and Provost is sat",1879e4a0-c6c1-4ad9-b5b2-c1cb75b72da7,0.4508,0.2817,0.0302,"Disciplinary action shall be just and reasonable and
be commensurate with the offense.
5.75.2 ""Cause"" for disciplinary measures shall include:
(a) Serious unprofessional behaviour.
(b) Failure to comply with any of the provisions of this Collective Agreement, minor technical violations excepted.
5.75.3 The following are the only formal ""Disciplinary
Measures"" which may be taken by the Employer against a Member:
(a) A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the pe","According to the collective agreement, disciplinary action against a member must be just and reasonable and commensurate with the offense. The following are the only formal ""Disciplinary Measures"" that may be taken by the Employer against a Member:

1. A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the personnel file (5.75.3(a)).
2. The withholding of an annual increment (5.75.3(b)).
3. The suspension without pay; the reduction in pay shall be computed as one two hundred and sixtieth (1/260) of normal salary per day of suspension (5.75.3(c)).
4. The suspension with pay; if and only if the Vice-President, Academic cites the suspension with pay as a disciplinary measure (5.75.3(d)).
5. Dismissal of a Member for just cause as per Article 5.80 – Dismissal Procedures (5.75.3(e)).

Additionally, the collective agreement provides that:

* Disciplinary action must be based on progressive discipline, except in egregious cases (Section 5.75.2).
* Just cause for disciplinary measures includes serious unprofessional behaviour and/or misconduct constituting a grave and direct violation of personal safety, or persistent failure to discharge academic responsibility (Section 5.75.2(a) and (b)).
* Discipline shall be imposed only in compliance with principles of natural justice and due process (Section 5.75.4).
* Members have a fundamental right to know the nature of the allegations against them and the right to respond to such allegations (Section 5.75.5).

The collective agreement also outlines procedures for investigating and imposing discipline, including timelines for notification and meetings with the member and union representative.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,3.0055,2.8181,151.9922,4669.0,392.7,,,,bridge
