A study leave may be granted to a tenured, probatio","According to the agreement, study leaves can only be granted to:

* Tenured Members after 2 years of full-time service (Article 7.30.1)
* Probationary or Master Lecturer Members after 2 years of full-time service, but no sooner than 2 years after a sabbatical leave (Article 7.30.1)

Additionally, study leaves must be in the best interests of the University and must not exceed a maximum length of 2 years during a Member's academic career (Article 7.30).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.3581,3.0283,19.564,4671.0,390.8,,,,bridge
