Collective Agreement 2011-14
The Member could collect her/his pension in addition to the incentive if she/he so desired. If t","The collective agreement provides various provisions related to retirement, including:

1. Pension Plan amendments: The agreement states that no amendments to the Pension Plan can be made without LUFA's consent (5.90.5).
2. Defined Benefit and Supplementary Pension Plans: Members' contributions shall only be used toward funding the Defined Benefit component of the Retirement Plan, with all pension service contributions and benefits accrued prior to July 1, 2011, remaining in the hybrid component of the plan (8.45.3). Eligible Members participate in both the Retirement Plan and the Supplementary Pension Plan.
3. Employer contributions: The Employer's contributions to the Retirement Plan shall be at least the amount required to fund current service costs, unfunded liabilities, and solvency liabilities, or 7.5% of the unfunded liabilities, whichever is greater (8.45.4).
4. Interest on plan contributions: The Plan will be credited at the Plan rate of return, with interest credited at this rate (8.45.3).
5. Special Voluntary Early Retirement (SuVP): Members can participate in SuVP, which allows them to retire early and receive a pension incentive. Benefits and Pension contributions terminate upon death or the end of the month of retirement.
6. Roll-over amount: The allowable roll-over amount may be spread over the years of the SuVP, with the remaining incentive amount considered income for calculating the annual RRSP contribution limit.
7. CPP benefits: Members who contribute to the plan and are at least 60 years old may be eligible for full or partial CPP benefits.

These provisions outline the terms and conditions related to retirement under the collective agreement.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.8436,2.8262,162.1994,4669.0,397.1,,,,bridge
