Academics except for specific clauses within this section that clearly appl",ebfc7453-86f6-41d8-8af7-c7ea61a59bf7,0.4349,0.3805,0.0159,"ARTICLE 1 - PURPOSE AND DEFINITIONS
1.01 It is the purpose ofthis Collective Agreement to set forth the terms and conditions ofemployment and other specific
contractual provisions, to promote and maintain harmonious relationships between the Parties, to facilitate the Parties in
working together to encourage the development ofresearch and teaching necessary for the provision ofhigh quality
education to students, and to provide a means for settling such disputes as may arise from time to time.","According to Article 2.00 - RIGHTS, RESPONSIBILITIES AND DUTIES OF ACADEMICS in the Collective Agreement:

Members of the bargaining unit have rights, duties and responsibilities which derive from their positions as teachers/professional librarians and scholars working within the University community, and which reflect the reasonable expectations of the Members, the University community and the contractual expectations of the Employer.

Specifically, members have the right to engage in various activities such as:

A. Teaching / Professional Librarianship / Archives Management
B. Scholarly Activity
C. University Governance and Administrative Duties
D. Outside Professional Activities
E. Service to the Community
F. Other Paid Activity

The agreement also outlines that members' responsibilities vary between two streams: Regular Stream and Alternate Stream.

For Regular Stream members, they have responsibilities relating to items A), B) and C), and are expected to participate actively in these areas, although not necessarily in all three in any one given year.

For Alternate Stream members, they have responsibilities relating to items A) and C), and are expected to participate actively in these areas, although not necessarily in both in any one given year.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.8631,2.9213,199.8104,4669.0,326.4,,,,bridge
