the patents and copyright articles of this Collective Agreement.","According to Article 2.55 of the Collective Agreement, a Joint Consultative Committee (JCC) is established to ""conduct such business as is referred to it."" However, specific roles and responsibilities are not explicitly defined in this article.

To find more information on the Joint Consultative Committee, we need to look at other sections of the agreement or relevant Labour Relations Acts. Section 113 of the Ontario Labour Relations Act, 1995 is referenced in Article 2.55, but it only provides a general framework for notices and does not explicitly define the JCC's role.

