Department(s","According to Article 11, the rules concerning redundancy are as follows:

1. A redundancy is defined as a situation where the Employer declares it (Article 11.10.2).
2. The Employer must declare a state of redundancy by sending a written notice to the Union and to the Vice-President Academic.
3. Redundancy does not apply to limited-term appointments with no implication of renewal or continuation (Article 5.20 – Appointment and Renewal).
4. If the proposed reductions will result in insufficient academic personnel for that Department/School to continue offering a viable program, the Employer shall not declare a redundancy (Article 11.10).
5. The onus lies with the Employer to show that the proposed reductions are consistent with normal workloads as defined in Article 5.40 – Academic Workload.

Additionally, if a program involves more than one Faculty or Department/School, the decision to approve or reject a program redundancy is made by the Board after hearing a submission from the Vice-President, Academic (Article 11.10.b).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.2311,2.8677,30.6528,4671.0,397.0,,,,bridge
