ARTICLE 8.15 – PROGRESS-THROUGH-THE-RANKS INCREMENTS
8.15.1 The purpose of these increm","According to the Collective Agreement 2008-11:

1. Merit increments are awarded by the Vice-President, Academic and become a permanent part of the Member's salary structure (Article 8.25.1).
2. Only Full Professors/Librarians and Permanent Sessional Lecturers are eligible for merit increments (Article 8.25.1).
3. The goal is to award merit increments to at least five percent (5%) of the Full Professors/Librarians and Permanent Sessional Lecturers at Laurentian University, but this does not mean that the criteria specified in clause 8.25.5 will be violated (Article 8.25.2).
4. Merit increments have a value of one Progress-Through-The-Ranks increment (Article 8.25.3).
5. Merit increments are awarded according to the procedures of Article 5.50 – Assessment of a Member’s Performance, and only tenured members are eligible to vote (Article 8.25.4).
6. For Full Professors/Librarians, the FPC/FFPC/LPC shall consider the award of merit increments in relation to criteria for promotion to the rank for Full Professor/Librarian (Article 8.25.5).

Additionally, it's mentioned that:

* The determination of individuals to receive merit increments is not subject to grievance (Article 4.20 - MERIT INCREMENTS, note: actually Article 4.21 is the one discussing Merit Increments, but I found this relevant).
* Progress-Through-The-Ranks increments have a value of $2,900 (Article 8.15.1).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.2319,3.1605,160.0901,4669.0,396.6,,,,bridge
