2021-2022 as described in Article 8.20 – Procedures for the Award/Denial of a Progress-Through-
The-Ranks Incr","The rules concerning the salary structure are outlined in Articles 8.10 and subsequent articles, which provide detailed information on how salaries are composed, increased or decreased, and awarded for promotions, additional qualifications, and merit increments.

Here are some key points:

* The salary of each Member is composed of a base salary modified by various items, including:
	+ Scale increases (Article 8.10.3)
	+ Progress-Through-The-Ranks increments (Article 8.15)
	+ Additional qualification increments (Article 8.30)
	+ Merit increments (Article 8.25)
* Salary increases or decreases are subject to certain conditions, such as the existence of a salary ceiling or floor.
* For all ranks, where a Member's salary exceeds $156,594 per annum, the PTR will be at 50% value.
* For all ranks, where a Member's salary exceeds $173,328 per annum, the PTR will be nil.
* Promotion increments are awarded according to Article 8.15 - Progress-Through-The-Ranks Increments and Article 8.25 - Merit Increments, regardless of breakpoints.
* Additional qualification increments are awarded pursuant to Article 8.30 - Additional Qualifications Increments in an amount of $2,900.

The rules regarding salary structure can be found in the following articles:

* Collective Agreement 2015-2018: Articles A.01-A.03
* Collective Agreement 2011-14: Article 8.10 and subsequent articles

Please note that these rules may have changed since the ratification of the collective agreement, and it is always recommended to consult the most recent version of the agreement for the latest information.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.8298,3.2665,369.5457,4669.0,399.7,,,,bridge
