5.35.1 In the year the Collective Agreement is being negotiated, all new hires whose appointments are effective July 1 or
before the signing of a new Collective Agreement shall receive all increases in salary for that year that become effective
July 1, except for the PTR increment, merit increment, or any other increase explicitly excluded by the new Collective
Agreement, irrespective of the actual date of commencement of employment. ARTICLE 5.40 – ACADEMIC WOR","According to Article 10.07 of the Collective Agreement 2017-2020, the President must ensure that the annual academic workload is determined, distributed, and scheduled as equitably as possible.

Specifically, the member's assigned annual academic workload must take into account the four domains of activity indicated in Section 10.01, as well as factors such as:

* The needs of the member's program, including student enrolments and the necessity of offering required courses (Article 10.07(a))

This implies that the collective agreement acknowledges the importance of considering the specific requirements of each academic program when determining the annual workload, in order to ensure equity and fairness for all members.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.281,2.9142,21.6131,4671.0,398.8,,,,bridge
