health, safety and security of Members as they carry out their duties. The Employer will
provide a copy of the annual report of the Health and Safety Committee to the Membership.
LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020 5
<<>>","According to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement, health, safety, and security are addressed through the following provisions:

1. The Employer recognizes a responsibility to provide an environment intended to protect the health, safety, and security of employees (ARTICLE 3.25.1).
2. The Employer agrees to maintain a Joint Health and Safety Committee, which will independently consider matters concerning the health, safety, and security of members.
3. The Employer is bound by the Occupational Health and Safety Act R.S.O 1990 as revised and in effect July 1, 2008 (ARTICLE 3.25.1).
4. The Employer recognizes its responsibility to provide an environment intended to protect the health, safety, and security of Members as they carry out their duties (ARTICLE 4.03).
5. A copy of the annual report of the Health and Safety Committee will be provided to the Membership.

These provisions emphasize the Employer's commitment to providing a safe working environment and its responsibility to maintain open communication with employees regarding health, safety, and security concerns.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.1892,2.8127,30.7356,4671.0,395.6,,,,bridge
