8.45.10 Benefits for","Unfortunately, the provided text snippet does not mention ""tuition fee exemption"" or any similar term. However, it does mention ""Fringe Benefits"".

According to Article 6.40 – FRINGE BENEFITS:

* ""Available Fringe Benefits"": The Employer agrees to maintain for its Members the same benefits package and cost-sharing basis available to the Association Members at Laurentian University of Sudbury.
* There is no specific mention of tuition fee exemption.

Regarding ""spousal"" benefits, there is also no direct mention in the provided text snippet. However, Article 6.40 also mentions ""Hospital Care and Extended Medical"", which may be related to spousal coverage under certain circumstances.

If you're looking for information on spousal benefits or tuition fee exemption, I recommend reviewing the full Collective Agreement 2011-14 or consulting with a relevant authority for more detailed information.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.8521,3.1468,27.6703,4671.0,394.6,,,,bridge
