(c) Cette étape ne peut être utilisée pour différer l'arbitrage d’une cause.","According to Article 11.15 of the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement, the arbitration procedure is defined as follows:

* The proceedings will be expedited by the Parties.
* The decision of the majority of the arbitrators and, where there is no majority, the decision of the chairperson will be final and binding upon the Parties and the Employee(s) concerned.
* Each Party will bear the expenses of the nominee appointed by it, and the Parties will share equally the fees and expenses, if any, of the Arbitrator chairperson of the Arbitration Board.
* The arbitrator shall not make any decisions inconsistent with the provisions of this Collective Agreement, nor alter, modify, add to, or amend any part of this Collective Agreement.
* No matter may be submitted to arbitration which has not been properly carried through all requisite steps of the Grievance Procedure hereinbefore set out unless otherwise agreed to in writing between the Parties.

Additionally, if no agreement is reached within 15 working days, either Party may request the Minister of Labour to appoint an arbitrator.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.8114,2.4299,217.011,4671.0,400.7,,,,bridge
