Article 7.25.9 (a) above, the University may grant up to a maximum of one (1) year of study le",21b6ddf0-d953-40a7-b1aa-576c6a56c4c1,0.4746,0.3797,0.0159,"ARTICLE 13 – STUDY LEAVE
13.01 A study leave with pay is granted to enable a member to pursue a program of study of benefit to the member and in
order to meet specific needs of the University. Study leave periods may vary. Vacation entitlement shall be proportional to
the length of the leave.","According to the agreement:

1. A study leave with pay is granted to enable a member to pursue a program of study that benefits the member and meets specific needs of the University (Article 13.01).
2. Study leave periods may vary.
3. Vacation entitlement shall be proportional to the length of the leave (Article 13.01).
4. When Members fail to submit their report, sabbatical credit will not begin to accumulate until January 1 or July 1, whichever is the closest date next following submission of the report (Article 13.01).
5. If, after reviewing the report, the Dean/University Librarian finds the performance to be unsatisfactory, appropriate measures may be taken, as provided in Article 5.75 – Disciplinary Measures (Article 13.01).

Additionally, there are specific provisions for Members on sabbatical leave who become disabled and cannot fulfill their sabbatical obligations, including:

* The Member must advise the Dean/University Librarian of the disability and provide a physician's report outlining the extent of the disability and expected date of return (Article 7.25.10).
* If the Member is disabled from performing tasks for less than 50% of the sabbatical leave, they are deemed to have taken their sabbatical leave.
* If the Member is disabled from performing tasks for more than 50% of the sabbatical leave, they are deemed not to have taken a sabbatical leave and are eligible to take it at the first mutually acceptable time (Article 7.25.10).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.2486,3.0601,122.0063,4669.0,403.5,,,,bridge
