12.13 A member on sabbatical leave shall continue, subject to the terms of such policies, to be covered by the
University’s group benefit plans, and the Employer shall continue its normal contributions toward the premium costs for
such plans.","According to the context provided, there are two conditions that apply to sabbatical leave:

1. The length of the sabbatical leave: A sabbatical leave is 12 months long, starting on July 1st, or 6 months long, starting on either July 1st or January 1st.
2. Workload and participation during the leave: Members who are on sabbatical leave and elect to remain on campus for all or part of the duration of the leave shall not normally be assigned any formal workload nor participate in any formal activities of the University, except those required by the Collective Agreement.

These conditions are mentioned in Article 22.07 of the source document.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.873,2.3447,21.0671,4669.0,331.0,,,,bridge
