materials. Such materials shall not be published, licensed, or released in any way, or amended, edited, cut, or in a",d5d7ea06-2261-48e3-894b-01fa33b47e2d,0.0164,0.016,0.0164,"A copy of the contract between the Member and
the University shall be sent to the Union.
6.35.3 If the University requests a work including a creative work, printed material, films, slides, tapes, computer
programmes, on-line course material, or similar materials from a Member under special contract, then, in the
absence of any agreement to the contrary, the University shall be the first owner of the copyright
therein. This includes all materials for distance education courses. A Member entering",72b525b2-9818-44fd-b4df-4bb3f1558f43,0.4454,0.3897,0.0161,"15.02 Vested in Member
Except where copyrightable materials are commissioned by the Employer,or produced for assessment, grading, report, or
correspondence pursuant to a member’s normal administrative and teaching duties within the University, the copyright to
all forms ofwritten, artistic, and recorded works shall be retained by the member(s) responsible for the origination ofthe
materials. Such materials shall not be published, licensed, or released in any way, or amended, edited, cut, or in a",cf2c6896-50a2-4be2-898a-fe84403a447c,0.0161,0.0157,0.0161,"A copy of the contract between the Member and the
University shall be sent to the Union.
6.35.3 If the University requests a work including a creative work, printed material, films, slides, tapes, computer
programmes, on-line course material, or similar materials from a Member under special contract, then, in the
absence of any agreement to the contrary, the University shall be the first owner of the copyright
therein. This includes all materials for distance education courses. A Member entering",06b25254-85c7-445a-842e-9099d85530f5,0.4463,0.357,0.0159,"ARTICLE 15 – COPYRIGHT
15.01 Copyright applies to all original written, artistic, and recorded works. Works include but are not limited to: books,
texts, articles, monographs, glossaries, bibliographies, cartographic materials, modular posters, study guides, laboratory
manuals, correspondence course packages, interactive textbooks, course work delivered on the Internet, multimedia
instructional packages, syllabi, tests and work papers, lectures, charts, transparencies, other visual aids, video a","According to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement, the rules concerning copyright are as follows:

* All members retain the copyright to their original written, artistic, and recorded works, except where specifically commissioned or produced by the Employer for assessment, grading, report, or correspondence purposes (Article 15.01).
* If a member produces a work under a special contract with the University, the University is considered the first owner of the copyright, including for distance education courses (6.35.3).
* A copy of the contract between the member and the University shall be sent to the Union.

It's also worth noting that certain works are explicitly excluded from the ""original written, artistic, and recorded works"" definition in Article 15.01, such as:

* Books
* Texts
* Articles
* Monographs
* Glossaries
* Bibliographies
* Cartographic materials
* Modular posters
* Study guides
* Laboratory manuals
* Correspondence course packages
* Interactive textbooks
* Course work delivered on the Internet
* Multimedia instructional packages
* Syllabi
* Tests and work papers
* Lectures
* Charts
* Transparencies
* Other visual aids
* Videos

These works are still subject to the provisions of Article 15.02, which governs the ownership of these materials in the absence of a specific agreement between the member and the University.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.7403,2.7719,39.5352,4671.0,407.7,,,,bridge
