10.30.1 Clinicians
Clinicians who have received 3 contracts within a 6 year period will be deemed to have Seniority, and shall
have priority of hire over external candidates. Available contracts will first be offered to individuals with the
most years of service. Where two members have equal years of service, the member with the most
cumulative months of service be awarded the contract. Individuals who are on an approved leave will continue to accrue active service time","There is no specific information provided about the withdrawal of seniority in the given context. The provided text only discusses the conditions for clinician seniority, as outlined in Article 10.30.1, but does not mention anything about withdrawing or revoking seniority. 

However, it can be mentioned that according to 4.40.5, the Council's determination may request that the Employer's seniority obligation to the Sessional Member be revoked.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.3484,2.92,16.551,4671.0,405.7,,,,bridge
