<<","According to Article 4.15 of the collective agreement, appointments of Sessional Lecturers are made by the Vice-President Academic and Provost or her/his designate on behalf of the Employer, on the recommendation of the Dean/University Librarian and the Department/School concerned.

The recommendation may be made by the Department/School as a whole, or by a committee consisting of no fewer than three (3) Members. Sessional appointments and other extra-departmental assignments of courses shall be made from rosters of names of potential instructors maintained by the Departments/Schools responsible for the particular course.

Sessional Members on the University roster shall be notified of the courses expected to be offered in their Department(s)/School(s) in all sessions of the upcoming year, with notice specified clearly. Sessional Members interested in teaching any of the available courses must send a letter of application by May 15, along with a current curriculum vitae, teaching dossier, and relevant supporting documentation.

Additionally, Sessions Members may have their names added to the rosters after this date, but seniority and other rights shall not be enforceable. Departments/Schools are allowed to advertise or solicit applications before or after the specified dates.

Full-time Members, previous and current Sessional Members, Retirees, and other qualified applicants may apply for overload appointments or sessional contracts when courses cannot be made part of full-time Members' normal teaching loads.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.314,3.0854,230.2985,4671.0,407.0,,,,bridge
