ARTICLE 4.10 – APPOINTMENT PROVISIONS FOR SESSIONAL MEMBERS
4.10.1 The Parties recognise that the University's mission is best served by a largely full-time faculty and that it is
not generally desirable to make sessional appointments a substitute for full-time faculty.
4.10.2 At the same time, the Parties recognise that sessional faculty add a significant level of diversity, expertise
and practical experience to the University, and their value must be recognised in the governa",a20a86db-4c0a-4cb6-9da6-247821f40ad9,0.4377,0.383,0.0159,"11.11 The roster shall include the member’s name, email address
(University account or other email as provided by the
Sessional member), courses taught. In October ofeach year,the roster shall be provided to the Chair ofeach
Department, Sessional Members identified on the roster and the Union.","According to Article 11.10, the Employer shall maintain a University roster that includes:

* The member's name
* Email address (University account or other email provided by the Sessional member)
* Courses taught

In October of each year, the roster must be provided to:

* The Chair of each Department
* Sessional Members identified on the roster
* The Union

It is also stated that a Sessional Member may be removed from the roster if they have rejected 2 courses in 2 successive years (Article 11.10) or failed to teach a course in 4 successive years, as outlined in Article 11.13.

(Source document: Collective Agreement between Laurentian University and the Union of Northern Ontario College and University Employees, Article 11.10 and 11.13)",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.7333,2.4375,23.9202,4671.0,407.1,,,,bridge
