received by the Me","Family responsibility is addressed in Article 7.60, which deals with parental leave. The article outlines the requirements and benefits for employees taking parental leave, including the need to give written notice to the employer at least two weeks prior to the start of the leave (Article 7.60.7), and the provision of top-up payments to ensure that the employee receives a certain level of earnings during the leave period (Article 7.60.6).

In terms of family responsibility, Article 25.09 mentions that a Member may elect to defer contractual decisions on reappointment or tenure/permanence by an equivalent period of time while on pregnancy or parental leave.

Additionally, if both parents are Members, they may share their paid periods of leave between them and not exceed the agreed upon threshold (Article 25.09).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,False,,,,,2.8449,2.8992,193.4367,4669.0,335.8,,,,bridge
