Collective Agreement the term ""scholarly activity"" means:
(a) Research directed towards a contribution to knowledge, and the dissemination of its results; and/or
(b) Participation in those academic activities that contribute to the enhancement, creation and dissemination of
knowledge; and/or
(c)","Research and Development Support is addressed in Article 6.20 and 6.25 of the Collective Agreement.

Article 6.20 describes various initiatives to support faculty members, including:

* A minimum Start-up Grant of $8,000 for new full-time members with probationary or tenured appointments (Article 6.20.1)
* Recipients of this award have three years to use the funds, and any unspent amount is returned to the Office of the Vice-President, Academic and Provost after a three-year period (Article 6.20.2)

Article 6.25 addresses the Laurentian University Research Fund (LURF), which provides research funding to faculty members through an open competition among members. The LURF includes:

* An annual research fund of $160,000 for each year of the Collective Agreement (Article 6.25.1)
* Additional funding of $20,000 per year to support both research activities and attendance at academic and professional conferences by retired Members (Article 6.25.2)
* A LURF Committee composed of eight full-time members evaluates proposals submitted to the Research, Creativity and Development Office once a year (Article 6.25.3)",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.3221,2.8369,260.5905,4669.0,411.3,,,,bridge
