D","According to the provided context, the collective agreement states that:

* The Employer retains the right to appoint Senior Academic Administrators.
* However, the Employer recognizes the usefulness and desirability of consultation with Members and Departments in their selection and appointment. (Article 11.28)
* Senior Academic Administrators who are excluded from the bargaining unit by virtue of their office must return to take-up membership upon resignation/retirement/removal from that office. (Article ?)
* No Member shall be displaced from the unit by the entry or re-entry of former senior Academic Administrators.

