7.35.1 The Employer and the Union endorse the principle of voluntary reduced workload as being mutua","The Collective Agreement 2017-2020 defines ""voluntary reduced workload"" (Article 7.35) as:

""...the reduction of a full-time Member's workload on an agreed-upon schedule, with proportionate reductions in pay and benefits...""

In other words, voluntary reduced workload refers to a mutually agreed upon arrangement between the employee and the Employer where the employee reduces their work hours or workload on a scheduled basis, resulting in a corresponding reduction in pay and benefits.

