5.20.27 All Adjunct faculty Members shall also be included in the faculty lis","According to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement:

1. The process of developing recommendations on faculty appointments is a peer-review process (LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2012-2016, Article 13.01).
2. The Employer determines the faculty complement necessary to carry out its objectives and mission, and final decisions are the responsibility of the Board and President (LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2012-2016, Article 13.01).
3. If a number of candidates have been judged to be substantially equal in qualifications and appropriateness of academic specialization, priority is given to Canadian citizens, permanent residents, and persons on minister's permits (2017-2020 Thorneloe-LUFA Collective Agreement, Section 4.a)).
4. In disciplines where it's difficult to attract qualified faculty, relevant criteria for appointment include teaching/professional, scholarly potential, and employment equity goals (2017-2020 Thorneloe-LUFA Collective Agreement, Section 4.b)).

Note that the collective agreement also mentions priority consideration for members from the roster in sessional appointments (11.14) but does not provide further details on this aspect.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.8458,3.1595,33.9649,4671.0,411.3,,,,bridge
