Librarian shall follow the criteria for establishment and seniority listed in clauses 4.15.12 to 4.15.21 below, and for
overloads in paragraph 5.40.6 (b) of
Article 5.40 – Academic Workload.
4.15.8 During October of each year the Employer will circulate to all Departments/Schools, the Union and the Library a list
of courses taught on an overload basis by full-time Members of facult","Overloads are stated in Article 6.30 — Overloads and Article 4.80.06 Voluntary Overload Teaching. Here are the key points:

* Voluntary overload teaching requires written agreement between the Employer (University) and the Member.
* The written agreement shall include course number and cancellation conditions.
* Rates of pay for overload teaching are stated in Article 6.30 — Overloads.
* Inequitable workloads are created when a Member voluntarily agrees to perform extra teaching without compensation by overload stipends.
* Members may be assigned teaching duties outside the on-campus Winter session, but such assignments shall be made on a fair and equitable basis and not more than once every three years.

Additionally, Article 4.80.06 Voluntary Overload Teaching states that voluntary overload teaching is any teaching additional to that stated in the assigned workload.

It's worth noting that overloads are also discussed in other articles, such as Article 5.40 – Academic Workload and Article 8.35 – Overloads, which govern the establishment and seniority of sessional members and provide criteria for determining workloads.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.7457,2.6614,136.6551,4669.0,414.1,,,,bridge
