(a) Serious unprofessional behaviour.
(b) Failure to comply with any of the provisions of this Collective Agreement, minor technical violations excepted.
5.75.3 The following are the only formal ""Disciplinary
Measures"" which may be taken by the Employer against a Member:
(a) A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the pe","According to the provided text, the following information is stated about discipline:

* Discipline shall be just and reasonable (5.75.2)
* Discipline shall be commensurate with the offense (5.75.3)
* Just cause for disciplinary measures includes:
 * Serious unprofessional behaviour (5.75.2(a))
 * Failure to comply with any of the provisions of this Collective Agreement, minor technical violations excepted (5.75.2(b))
* The following are the only formal ""Disciplinary Measures"" that may be taken by the Employer against a Member:
 1. A letter of reprimand (5.75.3(a))
 2. The withholding of an annual increment (5.75.3(b))
 3. The suspension without pay (5.75.3(c))
 4. The suspension with pay, if and only if the Vice-President, Academic cites it as a disciplinary measure (5.75.3(d))
 5. Dismissal for just cause (5.80)
* Discipline shall be imposed in accordance with principles of natural justice and due process
* Members have the right to know the nature of the allegations against them and the right to respond to such allegations
* Cases involving non-culpable behaviour by a Member as a result of physical or mental illness shall be treated separately from cases for disciplinary conduct

Note that this information is specific to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,3,True,,,,,2.2501,2.2992,252.1285,4669.0,410.3,,,,bridge
