ARTICLE 3.10 – LIBERTÉ UNIVERSITAIRE
3.10.1 En plus des droits de citoyen que leur confèrent les lois, les Membres joui","The relevant section of the Collective Agreement 2018-2021 is Section 0.02 Academic freedom and Section 11.02 Rights and Responsibilities as Full-Time Teachers/Librarians.

Regarding your question, there is no specific provision in the provided excerpts that directly addresses ""permission reasonable"". However, Section 3.10.1 of the Collective Agreement states:

""En plus des droits de citoyen que leur confèrent les lois, les Membres jouissent également d'une liberté universitaire qui leur permet de rechercher et de développer leurs connaissances et leurs idées de manière libre.""

Translated to English, it reads:

""In addition to the citizen rights that they confer through laws, Members also enjoy a university freedom that allows them to research and develop their knowledge and ideas in a free manner.""

This section emphasizes the importance of academic freedom, but does not specifically address ""reasonable permission"".",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.9574,3.1765,28.5147,4669.0,410.8,,,,bridge
