7.20.3 Any absence from campus affecti","According to Article 7.20 – ABSENCE - GENERAL, the agreement states that:

* The University requires its members' availability on a regular and ongoing basis to ensure the orderly conduct of scheduled and unscheduled activities (7.20.1).
* Any absence should not normally interfere with assigned and/or scheduled activities and the harmonious functioning of the Department/School (7.20.2).
* Absence from campus affecting teaching/professional librarian duties should be made up on a full pay basis, without loss of seniority or rights (no page number provided).

Note that there are two instances of 7.20.3 with different wording, but they appear to refer to the same requirement for making up absence related to teaching/professional librarian duties.",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.2546,2.8842,24.5784,4671.0,409.8,,,,bridge
