In ma","According to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement:

* The ballots shall be opened and counted in the presence of the Selection Committee (Article 9.15.9).
* The Chair of the Selection Committee shall report the results of the selection process and its recommendation to the Dean/University Librarian (Article 9.15.9).
* If the Dean/University Librarian is prepared to accept the Selection Committee's recommendation, they will forward this recommendation together with their own to the Vice-President, Academic, who will make the appointment (Article 9.15.10).
* If there is disagreement between the Dean/University Librarian and the Selection Committee regarding an appointment, the selection procedure shall be reinstated as in Article 9.15.3 above.
* The Chair/Director must be a tenured or probationary Member of faculty.

Additionally, in exceptional circumstances, the Vice-President, Academic and Provost and the Dean/University Librarian may appoint an acting Chair/Director for a period of up to four (4) months, consistent with Article 9.20 – Term of Office of Chairs/Directors and Article 9.30 – Removal from Office of Chairs/Directors (Article 9.15.13).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,3.1479,2.9578,37.5057,4669.0,349.1,,,,bridge
test_en_467,What are the rules concerning academic activity?,72eb11c0-2343-4dc8-90fd-9509b520f66c,0.4444,0.3889,0.0164,"ARTICLE 10 —ACADEMIC ACTIVITY
10.01 The Members ofthe bargaining unit, as academics, are committed to the transmission and creative expression of
knowledge, to the clarification and extension of its boundaries, to university governance, and to professional and
community service, They are entitled to and are expected to engage in the following activities, in a reasonable proportion
varying from individual to individual:
(a) the performance ofteaching duties as assigned according to this Collectiv",e97de394-168a-4b71-9912-9bffab519981,0.0164,0.0143,0.0164,"The dossier shall include: an up-to-date curriculum vitae that details the applicant’s scholarly research activity and
university and community service record; a teaching dossier along with Senate approved student course evaluations; any
other material that the applicant deems relevant.
(i) In addition to the documents submitted by the member, the committee will also consider the written evaluation from
tenure and tenure track members ofthe Department to be requested by the Chair ofthe Faculty A",a15f1ff4-c338-46b3-8d21-f538c146b81f,0.4444,0.3889,0.0161,"ARTICLE 10 —ACADEMIC ACTIVITY
