Article 7.25.9 (a) above, the University may grant up to a maximum of one (1) year of study le",82730778-bb1d-47ce-a70d-010aca9dd66b,0.5014,0.4011,0.0159,"ARTICLE 13 – STUDY LEAVE
13.01 A study leave with pay is granted to enable a member to pursue a program of study of benefit to the member and in
order to meet specific needs of the University. Study leave periods may vary. Vacation entitlement shall be proportional to
the length of the leave.","According to the Laurentian University Faculty Association collective agreement (LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020), here are some key points that apply to study leave:

1. Study leaves may vary in length up to a maximum of 12 months and can be renewable without compensation.
2. A member on study leave receives 30% of their salary, up to a maximum of $40,000 (Article 23.02).
3. Time spent on other types of leave with a period of more than six months does not count towards the eligibility requirements for three years of uninterrupted service or years of service for determining salary while on study leave.
4. Study leaves do not accrue sabbatical credit until January 1 or July 1, whichever is the closest date next following submission of the report (Article 23.01).
5. If a member fails to meet performance expectations while on study leave, the Dean/University Librarian may take disciplinary measures, as outlined in Article 5.75-Disciplinary Measures.

Let me know if you have any further questions!",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,1,True,,,,,2.9251,2.7003,31.4786,4671.0,349.1,,,,bridge
