Member has a fundamental right to know, in a timely manner, the nature of the allegations against him/her, and the right
to respond to such allegations.
5.75.5 The following are the only forms of discipline which may be taken by the Employer against a Member:
(a) A letter of reprimand, specifying the grounds and adding this reprimand to the personnel file;
(b) The suspension with pay; if and only if the Vice-President, Academic and
Provost cites the suspension with pay as a disc","The collective agreement provides the following regarding discipline:

* Discipline shall be only for cause (Article 5.75.1) and shall be just and reasonable, based on the principle of progressive discipline, except in egregious cases (Article 5.75.2).
* The following are the only forms of discipline that may be taken by the Employer against a Member: 
  * A letter of reprimand (Article 5.75.3(a));
  * Withholding of an annual increment (Article 5.75.3(b));
  * Suspension without pay (Article 5.75.3(c));
  * Suspension with pay, if and only if the Vice-President, Academic and Provost cites it as a disciplinary measure (Article 5.75.3(d));
  * Dismissal for just cause (Article 5.80.1).
* Prior to imposing discipline, the Employer shall meet with the Member and their Union representative within 20 working days of the conclusion of an investigation to review the matter with the Member (Article 5.75.7).
* The Member and their Union representative shall be given five working days' notice of the time and place of the meeting (Article 5.75.6 and 5.75.7).

Note: The agreement also provides separate procedures for cases involving sickness or disability, and for grievances regarding disciplinary measures against Sessional Members (Articles 5.75.8 and 5.75.10).",llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M,en,2,True,,,,,2.3695,2.7518,142.8479,4669.0,415.9,,,,bridge
